# Test: with no ze running, dump, fmt, graph and diff say an external plugin's section is not available
#
# Question: with no ze running, does each local inspection command, on a file
# that holds a section under an external plugin's own root, refuse the section,
# say a running ze was asked and none answered, and name one fix, without
# starting the plugin's program?
# Why not a unit test: TestInspectRouteFallsBackWhenNoZeAnswers proves the
# fallback over a stub ask. Only the real command shows the walk to the
# daemon's listener failing and its reason reaching the operator's refusal.
#
# The program the config declares writes a marker when it is started, so a
# command that ran it leaves the marker behind.
#
# VALIDATES: owner ruling of 2026-11-16 for the four commands: with no daemon
#   running, what needs an external plugin is not available, and the refusal
#   says what is true and names one fix.
# PREVENTS: a refusal that says no ze was asked after one was; a fix that names
#   `ze config validate` for a command that is not validate; a program started
#   with no daemon.

option=timeout:value=60s
option=env:var=ze.ssh.username:value=admin
option=env:var=ze.ssh.password:value=testpass
option=env:var=ze.ssh.port:value=$PORT

tmpfs=marker.run:terminator=EOF_RUN
#!/bin/sh
echo started > started-by-ze.marker
EOF_RUN

tmpfs=ze.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external acme-shell {
		run "sh marker.run"
		encoder json
	}
}

acme-shell {
	interval 5
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config dump ze.conf:exit=1
expect=stderr:contains=unknown top-level keyword: acme-shell
expect=stderr:contains=the config declares external plugin "acme-shell"
expect=stderr:contains=none answered: no ze listens at 127.0.0.1:
expect=stderr:contains=then `ze config dump ze.conf` again
expect=stderr:contains=fix: ze start
reject=stderr:contains=fix: ze config validate

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config fmt ze.conf:exit=2
expect=stderr:contains=unknown top-level keyword: acme-shell
expect=stderr:contains=none answered: no ze listens at 127.0.0.1:
expect=stderr:contains=then `ze config fmt ze.conf` again
expect=stderr:contains=fix: ze start
reject=stderr:contains=fix: ze config validate

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze config graph ze.conf:exit=2
expect=stderr:contains=unknown top-level keyword: acme-shell
expect=stderr:contains=none answered: no ze listens at 127.0.0.1:
expect=stderr:contains=then `ze config graph ze.conf` again
expect=stderr:contains=fix: ze start
reject=stderr:contains=fix: ze config validate

cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze config diff ze.conf ze.conf:exit=2
expect=stderr:contains=unknown top-level keyword: acme-shell
expect=stderr:contains=none answered: no ze listens at 127.0.0.1:
expect=stderr:contains=then `ze config diff ze.conf ze.conf` again
expect=stderr:contains=fix: ze start
reject=stderr:contains=fix: ze config validate

cmd=foreground:seq=5:exec=ze config dump ze.conf:exit=1
expect=file:path=started-by-ze.marker:absent=true
